DAY 54 - PART A: THEORY
GitOps with Argo CD
Time: 40 minutes
==================================================================

1. WHAT IS GITOPS?
------------------
  - The desired state of the cluster lives in GIT (YAML, Kustomize,
    Helm values).
  - An agent IN the cluster continuously PULLS from Git and applies
    changes (reconciliation loop, again!).
  - Nobody runs kubectl apply for deployments. To change the cluster,
    you change Git (pull request, review, merge).
  - Drift (someone runs kubectl edit) is detected and optionally
    reverted automatically.
Benefits: audit trail (git log), easy rollback (git revert), review,
CI doesn't need cluster credentials, disaster recovery = point a new
cluster at the repo.


2. ARGO CD
----------
Components: API server + UI, repo-server (renders Helm/Kustomize),
application-controller (compares and syncs), Redis, Dex (SSO).
Core object: Application

  apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
  kind: Application
  metadata:
    name: myapp-dev
    namespace: argocd
  spec:
    project: default
    source:
      repoURL: https://github.com/<you>/k8s-journey.git
      targetRevision: main
      path: week8/kustomize/overlays/dev
    destination:
      server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
      namespace: kz-dev
    syncPolicy:
      automated:
        prune: true       # delete things removed from Git
        selfHeal: true    # revert manual changes
      syncOptions:
      - CreateNamespace=true

Status: Sync (Synced/OutOfSync) + Health (Healthy/Progressing/Degraded).


3. PATTERNS
-----------
  App of apps / ApplicationSet   generate many Applications (per env,
                                 per cluster, per folder)
  Environments                   one folder/overlay per env; promote by
                                 changing the image tag in the next env
  Flux CD                        the other popular GitOps tool (CNCF),
                                 same ideas, no UI by default


KEY POINTS TO REMEMBER
----------------------
- Git is the source of truth; the cluster pulls.
- Argo CD Application = repo + path + destination + sync policy.
- prune + selfHeal keep the cluster equal to Git.
